 ## Subtopics
 
 ### Finish Unquantize
-This variant handles the interpolation between two unquantized endpoints using a weight. It is used when a value is not an endpoint but lies between them. It sets itself apart by performing a weighted average with specific fixed-point arithmetic adjustments (bias and scaling) to maintain precision during the interpolation process. Choose this when decoding interpolated values in block compression schemes. Link: [Finish Unquantize](5935-quantization.md#finish-unquantize) (hypothetical link within parent).
+Interpolates between two unquantized endpoints using a weight and converts to final float3. It is used when a voxel or texel value is derived from a blend of two base endpoints. Choose this when the compression scheme uses weighted interpolation (like BC6H) rather than direct endpoint selection. It differs from basic unquantization by handling the interpolation logic and final scaling to float32.
 
